\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Curvature of the fold}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{For the Morris–Lecar steady current in \ref{fnip-0076}, at a
fold the derivative of that current with respect to voltage is
zero. The second derivative is the curvature of the fold. The
applied current enters the voltage equation of \ref{fnip-0005}
through the reciprocal of #{C_{\mathrm{M}}}, so the derivative in
that parameter is nonzero. These are the two inequalities of \ref{fnip-0087}.
Both folds of the SNLC column satisfy them, and the quadratic
coefficient on the [center manifold](fnip-0059) is nonzero at each
fold.}
